  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This 2022 Figshare dataset is already showing early scholarly uptake, with 3 OpenAlex citations, 5 documented downstream reuse events, and 48 downloads. The citing record points to a focused but visible role in protist genomics and the study of close relatives of animals.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset provides draft and decontaminated metagenome assemblies for four eukaryotic species, along with genome annotations and predicted protein sequences for the cleaned assemblies. Its strongest impact signal is in research reuse: the record shows 5 downstream reuse events and 3 citations, indicating that the resource is being incorporated into follow-on genomics and evolutionary biology work rather than remaining only a static repository deposit.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citing landscape is especially concentrated in protist diversity and phylogeny, with citations appearing in Protist, eLife, Nature, and a bioRxiv preprint. That pattern suggests the dataset is relevant to high-visibility work on the biology and evolution of unicellular lineages, particularly studies addressing the closest living relatives of animals and broader questions in multicellularity and evolutionary history.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Usage data also support this picture of early interest: Figshare records 141 views and 48 downloads, which is a meaningful level of engagement for a specialized dataset. OpenAIRE identifies the record as openly accessible, and the repository metadata and related identifiers indicate that the dataset is being maintained in a way that supports discovery and reuse.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The surrounding evidence is still modest in scale, so the safest interpretation is that this is an emerging resource with clear domain-specific traction rather than a broadly diffuse one. There are no recorded online mentions in the available event-data sources, and the public-discourse and preprint-metrics feeds are unavailable in this record, so the clearest documented impact remains scholarly citation, reuse, and direct usage.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the dataset appears to serve as foundational genomic infrastructure for a specialized but influential research area. Its uptake in high-profile evolutionary and protistology venues suggests that it is contributing to a chain of analyses on early-branching eukaryotes and animal origins.</p>",
